    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nai, surround\n\n### Description\n\nFor vue, svelte or other template language, textobj \"at\" or \"it\"  only work for common tag without \"-\". For example div\r\n![图片](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23305067/235364482-16fe5b0b-b853-414a-9848-30f482c11a8f.png)\r\nBut for \"el-dropdown-menu\", it dones select  tag \"el-dropdown-menu\", but select the outer tag \"template\", because \"template\" has no \"-\"\r\n![图片](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23305067/235364668-236d51eb-b372-4f65-ae8d-0b36779e58d2.png)\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nuse \"vat\" or \"vit\" on html tag with \"-\"\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n![图片](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23305067/235364744-f106bd88-45e1-49c6-9f58-40dcef14e326.png)\r\n\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![图片](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23305067/235364755-1a6add9f-f2cb-4a82-aadb-0dc7a69486ec.png)\r\n",
