        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nYes, tag implementation in 'mini.ai' relies on an appropriate Lua patterns to match a tag region. I would strongly suggest using tree-sitter to get more proper information about tag structure. Something like how it this mentioned in [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212277863).\r\n\r\nHowever, you can still customize tag textobject to include punctuation in tag name by slightly modifying built-in one like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    t = { '<([%p%w]-)%f[^<%w][^<>]->.-</%1>', '^<.->().*()</[^/]->$' }\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-04-30T17:57:19Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/314#issuecomment-1529097699",
